IMPORT prelude

-- Adoption of Children Act 2022 (Singapore) -- who may adopt (ss 4, 5), which child may be adopted (s 6), the pre-application
-- requirements and the ASA (ss 11, 14, 20), consent and its dispensation (ss 26, 37), what the court must be satisfied of (s 42),
-- confidentiality (s 48), payments (ss 53, 55), placement before an ASA (s 57), and the maximum penalties for the offences
-- encoded (ss 48(4), 54(4), 55(3), 56(2), 57(5), 57(10)).
--
-- Edition: Act 20 of 2022, informal consolidation -- version in force from 15/10/2024, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ACA2022.txt (retrieved 2026-10-01, labelled "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The only
-- amendment annotation seen in the body is "[Act 31 of 2022 wef 15/10/2024]" (at s 66). The arrangement of sections at the top of
-- the deposit is offset by two from the body; this encoding follows the BODY's section numbers.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a prospective adopter,
-- birth parent, adoption agency or publisher meets. Not encoded: the Guardian-in-Adoption's appointment and affidavit (ss 8, 27,
-- 28), ASA variation, revocation and appeals (ss 15 to 19), interim and ancillary court powers (ss 31 to 35, 43, 45), the detail of
-- ss 38 to 41 (ill-treatment, care or protection), birth registration and the effects of an order (ss 44, 46, 47), s 51 (adverts
-- of children for adoption), enforcement powers (Part 7), Part 8 general provisions, and the transitional provisions (ss 58, 85).
-- Offences "prescribed by the regulations" (s 5(1)(d)) and the regulations' suitability factors (s 7) were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Adoption of Children Act 2022 -- adoption`

DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `applicant's age` IS A NUMBER
    `is male` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is habitually resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a conviction for a prescribed offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is within the prohibited degrees with the child` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Child HAS
    `child's age` IS A NUMBER
    `is female` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds only a visit, student or special pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is present unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or has been married` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `4 -- who may apply`

-- s 4(1): an application may only be made by (a) 2 individuals married to each other, where "(iii) both the individuals are
-- habitually resident in Singapore; and (iv) either or both the individuals are citizens of Singapore, or both individuals are
-- permanent residents of Singapore"; or (b) an individual who is habitually resident and "either a citizen or permanent resident".
-- s 4(2): jointly by the couple in (1)(a), or "solely by an individual mentioned in subsection (1)(b) who is not an individual
-- mentioned in subsection (1)(a)" -- a married person may not apply alone.
-- s 4(3): the residence and citizenship requirements "do not apply" to an application supported by a valid and favourable HSR
-- (a Home Study Report applied for before s 11 commenced).
-- (The validity of the marriage under s 4(1)(a)(i), (ii) is assumed for joint applicants and not modelled.)
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a citizen or PR habitually resident` IF
    `the applicant`'s `is habitually resident in Singapore`
    AND (`the applicant`'s `is a citizen` OR `the applicant`'s `is a permanent resident`)

GIVEN `first` IS AN Applicant, `second` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the couple meets the residence test` IF
    `first`'s `is habitually resident in Singapore`
    AND `second`'s `is habitually resident in Singapore`
    AND (    `first`'s `is a citizen`
          OR `second`'s `is a citizen`
          OR (`first`'s `is a permanent resident` AND `second`'s `is a permanent resident`))

§§ `5(1) -- who is ineligible`

-- s 5(1): ineligible where (a), (b) an applicant "is below 25 years of age" or "is less than 21 years older than the child before the
-- court"; (c) "the sole applicant is a male and the child before the court is a female"; (d) an applicant "has been convicted of an
-- offence prescribed by the regulations" (whenever committed).
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fails the age test` IF
       `the applicant`'s `applicant's age` LESS THAN 25
    OR `the applicant`'s `applicant's age` MINUS `the child`'s `child's age` LESS THAN 21

§§ `4, 5 -- eligibility and the section 5(2) exceptions`

-- s 5(2): despite ineligibility under s 5(1) or s 4 the court MAY make an order where
--   (a) "in a case where subsection (1)(a) or (b) applies" -- an applicant and the child are within the prohibited degrees of
--       consanguinity (this cures the AGE bars only);
--   (b) one spouse applies solely and the other spouse consents, or that consent is dispensed with (spouse cannot be found or is
--       incapable, or the couple are separated and living apart with the separation likely to be permanent);
--   (c) "in a case where subsection (1) applies or the requirements in section 4(1)(a)(iii) or (iv) or (b) are not met" -- special
--       circumstances justify an order "as an exceptional measure" (s 5(3): giving due consideration to whether the
--       Guardian-in-Adoption supports it).
-- Read literally, a sole male applicant with a female child is caught by (1)(c), which (2)(a) does not reach, so only special
-- circumstances help -- even where he is her relative. And a married person applying alone is barred by s 4(2)(b), which (2)(c)
-- does not mention, so only (2)(b) helps.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `the child` IS A Child, `has a valid favourable HSR` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is married` IS A BOOLEAN, `the spouse consents or consent is dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a sole application can succeed on eligibility` IF
        (    (NOT `fails the age test` `the applicant` `the child`)
          OR `the applicant`'s `is within the prohibited degrees with the child`
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the applicant`'s `is male` AND `the child`'s `is female`))
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    (NOT `the applicant`'s `has a conviction for a prescribed offence`)
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    `is a citizen or PR habitually resident` `the applicant`
          OR `has a valid favourable HSR`
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    (NOT `is married`)
          OR `the spouse consents or consent is dispensed with`)

GIVEN `first` IS AN Applicant, `second` IS AN Applicant, `the child` IS A Child, `has a valid favourable HSR` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a joint application can succeed on eligibility` IF
        (    ((NOT `fails the age test` `first` `the child`) AND (NOT `fails the age test` `second` `the child`))
          OR `first`'s `is within the prohibited degrees with the child`
          OR `second`'s `is within the prohibited degrees with the child`
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    ((NOT `first`'s `has a conviction for a prescribed offence`) AND (NOT `second`'s `has a conviction for a prescribed offence`))
          OR `special circumstances`)
    AND (    `the couple meets the residence test` `first` `second`
          OR `has a valid favourable HSR`
          OR `special circumstances`)

§§ `6 -- which child`

-- s 6(1): only a child "who is resident in Singapore"; (2) deemed NOT resident if on "a visit pass, a student's pass or a special
-- pass ... irrespective of the number of occasions the pass is issued", or if present unlawfully; (3) not a child "who is or has
-- been married". s 2: "child" means "an individual below 21 years of age".
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child may be adopted` IF
        `the child`'s `child's age` LESS THAN 21
    AND `the child`'s `is resident in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `holds only a visit, student or special pass`)
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `is present unlawfully`)
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `is or has been married`)

§§ `11, 14, 20 -- briefings and the ASA`

-- s 11: an individual may apply only if he or she "(a) has attended a pre-adoption briefing ... within the last 3 years; (b) has
-- attended a disclosure of adoptive status briefing ... within the last 3 years; and (c) holds a valid and favourable ASA".
-- s 20(1): an ASA "is valid for a period of 2 years starting on the date that it is issued", unless extended (s 15(5), 17(6)(c),
-- or by the Guardian-in-Adoption's notice under s 20(3)). Times are in whole months; "within the last 3 years" is read as at most
-- 36 months (an inference about the boundary).
GIVEN `months since issue` IS A NUMBER, `validity extended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ASA is in its validity period` IF
    `months since issue` LESS THAN 24 OR `validity extended`

GIVEN `months since pre-adoption briefing` IS A NUMBER, `months since disclosure briefing` IS A NUMBER,
      `ASA is favourable` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since ASA issued` IS A NUMBER, `ASA extended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may make an adoption application` IF
        `months since pre-adoption briefing` AT MOST 36
    AND `months since disclosure briefing` AT MOST 36
    AND `ASA is favourable`
    AND `the ASA is in its validity period` `months since ASA issued` `ASA extended`

-- s 14(2): "No application for an ASA may be made" unless the individual has "(a) resided in Singapore for a continuous period of at
-- least one year immediately preceding" the ASA application and "(b) attended a pre-adoption briefing".
GIVEN `months of continuous residence` IS A NUMBER, `attended pre-adoption briefing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for an ASA` IF
    `months of continuous residence` AT LEAST 12 AND `attended pre-adoption briefing`

§§ `26 -- valid consent`

-- s 26(2): consent "is not validly obtained unless" it is (a) given after the prescribed information and documents are provided;
-- (b) "in writing and in the form prescribed"; (c) "witnessed by 2 witnesses present at the same time, each of whom must have
-- attained 21 years of age"; (d) obtained under the other prescribed procedures; and (e) attested by a solicitor, commissioner for
-- oaths, notary public or other person authorised to administer oaths.
GIVEN `information provided first` IS A BOOLEAN, `in writing in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `number of witnesses present together` IS A NUMBER, `age of the younger witness` IS A NUMBER,
      `attested by an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent is validly obtained` IF
        `information provided first`
    AND `in writing in the prescribed form`
    AND `number of witnesses present together` AT LEAST 2
    AND `age of the younger witness` AT LEAST 21
    AND `attested by an authorised person`

§§ `37 -- dispensing with consent`

-- s 37(1): the court may dispense with a relevant person's consent on grounds including (b) abandonment, neglect or cannot be
-- found; (c) grievous hurt; (d) past ill-treatment before "the specified period" AND, by its end, not having taken reasonable steps
-- to resolve the circumstances; (e) the same for failure to provide suitable care; (f) a drug addict convicted on at least 2
-- separate occasions; (g) remand, imprisonment or detention; (h) incapacity (with a medical or psychiatric assessment, s 37(2));
-- (i) the consent "ought to be dispensed with" in the court's opinion.
-- s 37(4): the specified period is the period immediately preceding the application: "(a) where the child is below 3 years of age --
-- 12 months; (b) where the child is 3 years of age or older -- 24 months".
GIVEN `the child's age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the specified period in months` MEANS
    IF `the child's age in years` LESS THAN 3 THEN 12 ELSE 24

GIVEN `ill-treated the child before the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps to resolve it by the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ill-treatment ground is made out` IF
    `ill-treated the child before the specified period` AND (NOT `took reasonable steps to resolve it by the end of the period`)

GIVEN `is a drug addict` IS A BOOLEAN, `separate occasions convicted under the Misuse of Drugs Act` IS A NUMBER,
      `is thereby unable, unwilling or unlikely to care for the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the drug ground is made out` IF
        `is a drug addict`
    AND `separate occasions convicted under the Misuse of Drugs Act` AT LEAST 2
    AND `is thereby unable, unwilling or unlikely to care for the child`

§§ `25, 26, 42 -- before the order`

-- s 25: the court "must not make an adoption order" unless the application is served on every relevant person (unless dispensed
-- with, s 25(3)) and on the Guardian-in-Adoption. s 26(1): nor unless the consent of every relevant person "has either been validly
-- obtained or dispensed with". s 42(1): nor unless satisfied that (a) the consenting persons have "freely consented to and
-- understand" the order (a parent, that it will "permanently ... deprive him or her of his or her parental rights"); (b) the order
-- "will be for the welfare of the child"; (c) the applicants have "the appropriate character and fitness and are or is suitable".
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `eligible or excepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `served as required` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `every consent obtained or dispensed with` IS A BOOLEAN, `consents free and understood` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for the welfare of the child` IS A BOOLEAN, `applicants suitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make the adoption order` IF
        `the child may be adopted` `the child`
    AND `eligible or excepted`
    AND `served as required`
    AND `every consent obtained or dispensed with`
    AND `consents free and understood`
    AND `for the welfare of the child`
    AND `applicants suitable`

§§ `48 -- identifying an adopted child`

-- s 48(1): a person must not publish or broadcast anything likely to identify a protected person "as a child who was or is the
-- subject of an adoption application" -- whether or not an order was made, and "even after the protected person attains 21 years
-- of age". (2) Not where: (a) application successful and person under 21 -- the adoptive parent consents; (b) person 21 or over --
-- the person consents; (c) application unsuccessful and person under 21 -- a relevant person consents; (d) in any case -- the
-- Guardian-in-Adoption approves. (3)(c): nor does it prevent the protected person, with no proceedings pending, publishing about
-- himself or herself.
GIVEN `age of the protected person` IS A NUMBER, `application succeeded` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `adoptive parent consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `protected person consents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `relevant person consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `Guardian-in-Adoption approves` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `published by the protected person with no proceedings pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the identifying publication is lawful` IF
       `Guardian-in-Adoption approves`
    OR `published by the protected person with no proceedings pending`
    OR (`age of the protected person` AT LEAST 21 AND `protected person consents`)
    OR (`age of the protected person` LESS THAN 21 AND `application succeeded` AND `adoptive parent consents`)
    OR (`age of the protected person` LESS THAN 21 AND (NOT `application succeeded`) AND `relevant person consents`)

§§ `53 -- payments by applicants`

-- s 53(1): applies to "any payment or other reward in consideration of the adoption of a child or for any adoption-related service"
-- made or received by the applicants. (2): every such payment and agreement "is void and unenforceable unless (a) ... sanctioned by
-- the court; or (b) the adoption application in question is withdrawn or struck out". (3): sanction is sought "at the time that the
-- adoption application is made". The section draws no line between payments s 55 permits and those it forbids.
GIVEN `sanctioned by the court` IS A BOOLEAN, `application withdrawn or struck out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is enforceable` IF
    `sanctioned by the court` OR `application withdrawn or struck out`

§§ `55 -- permitted payments`

-- s 55(1): no person may make, give, receive or agree to any payment or reward "in consideration of an adoption in Singapore of a
-- child or for any adoption-related service" unless permitted by (2) "or approved by the Guardian-in-Adoption in any particular
-- case". (2)(a): payment to an AUTHORISED adoption agency for the pre-adoption briefing, the disclosure briefing, or the ASA
-- assessment; (b) payments to defray the mother's necessary care around delivery, delivery medical expenses, the child's subsistence
-- and medical needs, a caregiver, medical assessments, travel or accommodation for the custody transfer, and administration, legal
-- or application fees for immigration, birth registration or the adoption order; (c) anything prescribed.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `a briefing fee to an authorised agency`
    `an ASA assessment fee to an authorised agency`
    `a briefing fee to an unauthorised agency`
    `a matching fee to an agency`
    `the birth mother's delivery medical expenses`
    `a caregiver's cost for the child`
    `travel for the transfer of custody`
    `legal fees for the adoption order`
    `a cash gift to the birth parent`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment, `approved by the Guardian-in-Adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment is permitted` IF
        `approved by the Guardian-in-Adoption`
    OR  CONSIDER `the payment`
        WHEN `a briefing fee to an unauthorised agency` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a matching fee to an agency` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a cash gift to the birth parent` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `57 -- placement before an ASA`

-- s 57(1): unless (3) is met, a "potential adopter" must not reside with, or spend time considering whether to adopt, a child for
-- whom an adoptive parent is being sought. (3): (a) child a citizen or PR -- the potential adopter "holds a valid and favourable
-- ASA"; (b) otherwise -- the ASA AND a dependant's pass for adoption, or its in-principle approval. (4) Not where (a) the adopter or
-- spouse and the child are within the prohibited degrees of consanguinity; (b) a stepchild; (c) a care-giver under a voluntary
-- care agreement or CYPA order; (d) prescribed; (e) "permitted by the Guardian-in-Adoption". s 57(11): "potential adopter" includes
-- anyone who has merely "communicated to a relevant person of a child that the individual desires to adopt the child".
GIVEN `child is a citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid favourable ASA` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dependant's pass or in-principle approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `related within the prohibited degrees` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a stepchild` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a CYPA care-giver` IS A BOOLEAN, `permitted by the Guardian-in-Adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the potential adopter may reside with the child` IF
       `related within the prohibited degrees`
    OR `is a stepchild`
    OR `is a CYPA care-giver`
    OR `permitted by the Guardian-in-Adoption`
    OR (`child is a citizen or PR` AND `holds a valid favourable ASA`)
    OR ((NOT `child is a citizen or PR`) AND `holds a valid favourable ASA` AND `dependant's pass or in-principle approval`)

§§ `48(4), 54(4), 55(3), 56(2), 57(5), 57(10) -- maximum penalties`

-- s 48(4): fine up to $5,000; second or subsequent conviction up to $10,000 (no imprisonment).
-- s 54(4) (agency fee list, without reasonable excuse): $5,000 or 12 months or both; second or subsequent $10,000 or 12 months.
-- s 55(3) (non-permitted payment), s 56(2) (fraud, duress or undue influence to obtain consent or custody), s 57(5) (placement) and
-- s 57(10) (failing to obey a delivery order): $10,000 or 3 years or both; second or subsequent $20,000 or 6 years or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `identifying publication under s 48`
    `agency fee list breach under s 54`
    `non-permitted payment under s 55`
    `improper inducement under s 56`
    `unlawful placement under s 57(5)`
    `disobeying a delivery order under s 57(10)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `identifying publication under s 48` THEN IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    WHEN `agency fee list breach under s 54` THEN IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    OTHERWISE IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `is a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `identifying publication under s 48` THEN 0
    WHEN `agency fee list breach under s 54` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE IF `is a repeat conviction` THEN 72 ELSE 36
